  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-03 (concurrent run, not merged): branch jgstern-agent/fix/nakur (worktree ~/hg_wt/nakur), commit a56cc21c1b. Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/nakur.md.\n\n- Premise reproduced first (the item's own mutation check): with \"dart\" and \"javascript\" removed from type-hierarchy-linker's clause, test_depends_on_producer_sets.py ran 1 failed / 39 passed and the only failure was the exact-value pin; test_every_direct_analyzer_emitter_is_declared stayed GREEN.\n- Fix: option (b)-family, but general rather than dict-specific. New hypergumbo_core.value_flow follows a value back through the module (loop/comprehension targets, tuple positions, appended/stored/extended elements, local returns/yields, private/nested function parameters via all call sites, record-class fields, IfExp narrowing), answering only when every route was followed. producer_coherence._classify_value falls back to it; new scan_file_emits/FileEmits per-module core. The depends_on scan now uses that shared classifier and pins the analyzer sites it cannot enumerate (only yaml_ansible's edge.edge_type copy).\n- Option (a) (behavioural fixtures) was not taken: it covers only languages with a fixture, and rust_analyzer/scip_python need external binaries.\n- Same mutation AFTER the fix: test_every_direct_analyzer_emitter_is_declared RED with ['dart', 'javascript']. With the value_flow fallback disabled (M1), the new scanner test is red on dart and the closed-world test lists dart/js_ts/smithy sites.\n- First catch: kotlin emits extends/implements itself (live repro: Square->Base extends, Square->Shape implements, origin kotlin, type-hierarchy builds dispatches_to from them) and was not declared; now declared.\n- NOT covered: the scan is per-module, so rust_analyzer/scip_python (edges emitted in core scip/edges.py) remain hand-declared; residuals filed as WI-gajoz-fasad-vojih-gomup-domar-zivis-durok-rudin.\n- Tests: targeted smart-test on the 3-commit branch: 22245 passed, 4 skipped, 10 xfailed, 0 failed (637 files), all 7 changed sources at 100% coverage; plus 142 passed on the unselected axis/concept-axes tests."  # efd6
